base.txt / dev.txt / prod.txt  - what the portal needs, as version ranges.
prod.lock                      - what production actually installs: every
                                 package pinned to one version with the sha256
                                 of every distribution file. The Dockerfile
                                 installs from this with --require-hashes.

Regenerate the lock whenever a range in base.txt or prod.txt changes:

    pip install pip-tools
    pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file requirements/prod.lock requirements/prod.txt

Commit the lock with the change that needed it. A build that fails on a hash
mismatch is the lock doing its job - re-run the command above, do not delete
the offending lines.
